TITLE:: LeftCommand
SUMMARY:: Command that moves selected notes left by a beat subdivision.
CATEGORIES:: Commands
RELATED:: Classes/Command, Classes/Parameter, Classes/CommandPrompt, Classes/PianoRoll, Classes/PianoRollNote, Classes/RightCommand, Classes/SnapCommand

DESCRIPTION::
TELETYPE::LeftCommand:: is a LINK::Classes/Command:: named CODE::left:: that moves each selected note left by a beat subdivision. LINK::Classes/PianoRoll:: supplies the notes through LINK::Classes/CommandPrompt#-ambientParameters:: as CODE::selectedNotes::.

CODE::resolution:: is a positive integer from 1 to 16, the same fractions of a beat as LINK::Classes/SnapCommand::. The step size is CODE::1.0 / resolution:: beats:
LIST::
## CODE::1::: Whole beat (1.0 beat)
## CODE::2::: Half beat (0.5 beats)
## CODE::4::: Quarter beat (0.25 beats)
## CODE::8::: Eighth beat (0.125 beats)
## CODE::16::: Sixteenth beat (0.0625 beats)
::

A note already on that grid moves one step left. A note off the grid moves to the adjacent grid line to the left. Duration is preserved. Start time is clamped at beat zero. LINK::Classes/PianoRollNote#-nudgeLeft:: repositions the note view.

CLASSMETHODS::

METHOD:: new
Creates a new TELETYPE::LeftCommand::. Takes no arguments; movement is applied by LINK::#-execute::.

RETURNS::
A new TELETYPE::LeftCommand:: instance.

INSTANCEMETHODS::

METHOD:: execute
Moves each note in CODE::\selectedNotes:: left by the grid implied by CODE::\resolution::.

ARGUMENT:: args
A LINK::Classes/Dictionary:: or LINK::Classes/Event:: with CODE::\selectedNotes:: (an LINK::Classes/Array:: of notes that respond to CODE::nudgeLeft::) and CODE::\resolution:: (an LINK::Classes/Integer:: from 1 to 16).

EXAMPLES::

CODE::
(
var note = PianoRollNote(1.0, 60, 100,
	viewFunc: { View() },
	selectFunc: {},
	deselectFunc: {},
	setPart1Func: {},
	setPart2Func: {},
	setPart3Func: {},
	setPart4Func: {},
	moveFunc: { |view, start, stop| ("Moved to " ++ start ++ ".." ++ stop).postln; }
);
note.stop(2.0);

// Move left by a quarter beat (resolution = 4)
LeftCommand.new.execute((
	selectedNotes: [note],
	resolution: 4
));
)
::
